  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Sunday/...Onshore flow with at\ntimes moderate showers continue for Thursday with the stacked but\nweakening low lingering over the northern Gulf. The low will \nshift southeast and weaken further Thursday night into Friday, \nwith showers diminishing from north to south across the panhandle.\nAny lingering showers across the southern panhandle should by \nFriday afternoon. A few lingering snow showers possible for \nThursday along the Klondike Highway and the upper reaches of the \nHaines Highway but any accumulations would be minimal. As the low \ndeparts to the southeast, ensemble and deterministic guidance \ngenerally show upper-level ridge over mainland Alaska shifting \neast and settling over SEAK Friday into the weekend, with clearing\nskies and drier offshore flow developing. Gusty northerly winds \ncould develop along the northern highway into Lynn Canal. Daytime \nhighs will remain in the 40s throughout the period, with overnight\nlows in the 30s.",
